.TH GIT-WT 1 "August 24, 2026" "git-wt" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-wt \- manage and open project-oriented Git worktrees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git wt
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git wt
is an optional manual convenience for project-oriented Git worktrees.
With no command, it runs
.BR "git wt list" .
Writable lanes live beneath
.IR ~/worktrees/<owner>/<repository>/<lane> .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.I <branch>
Open or create a worktree for a branch.
.TP
.BI "issue " number " [--no-link-env]"
Create or reuse durable issue lane
.BR GH-<number> .
.TP
.BI "add " branch " [--no-link-env]"
Open an existing local or origin branch.
.TP
.BI "pr " number
Create or refresh detached inspection lane
.BR PR-<number> .
.TP
.BI "repair " number " [--no-link-env]"
Open a same-repository pull request's writable head branch.
.TP
.B list
List this clone's worktrees without pruning. This is the default command. The
interactive selector shows pull request titles in a flexible-width
.B TITLE
column while preserving complete
.B PATH
values; plain output retains its stable columns.
.TP
.B sync [--dry-run] [--json]
Reconcile origin and proven merged worktree lanes. An actual ignored
repository-root
.B bin/
directory is disposable build output during sync.
.TP
.B sweep [options]
Discover linked worktrees across built-in and configured roots, classify exact
GitHub merge evidence, report approximate disk usage, and offer bounded removal
actions. Bare terminal use prints grouped results and opens an action menu;
redirected output is non-mutating.
.TP
.B sweep config [--config path]
Create or update sweep configuration interactively. The first bare terminal
sweep offers the same wizard when the default config is absent. The wizard can
toggle built-ins, add or remove typed roots, preserve comments, display the
complete old/new YAML, retain one backup, and atomically write after final
confirmation. Operational automation, JSON, dry-run, and redirected runs never
prompt or create configuration.
.TP
.B home
Open a shell in this clone's primary worktree.
.TP
.B root
Print the canonical linked-worktree directory.
.TP
.BI "path " lane
Print an exact registered lane path for shell navigation.
.TP
.BI "cd " lane
Open an interactive shell in an exact registered lane.
.TP
.BI "remove " lane-or-path
Remove one exact clean, fully-pushed worktree.
.TP
.B prune [--dry-run]
Explicitly prune stale worktree metadata.
.TP
.B migrate [--apply]
Preview or apply legacy flat-directory migration.
.TP
.B help
Show command help.
.SH LIST OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--sort " attribute
Sort by
.BR updated ,
.BR state ,
.BR head ,
or
.BR path .
.TP
.BI "--root-position " position
Pin the primary worktree at
.B top
(the default) or
.BR bottom .
.TP
.B --reverse
Reverse the selected sort order.
.TP
.B --plain
Print the table instead of opening the terminal selector.
.SH SWEEP OPTIONS
.TP
.B --auto
Without prompting, remove only clean exact-head lanes proven merged into the
GitHub default branch plus native stale metadata.
.TP
.B --interactive, -i
Open the colorized multi-selector. Use arrows or j/k to move, Space to toggle,
/ to filter, s to sort, e to explain, and Enter to review. A second Enter
confirms the unchanged exact target set.
.TP
.B --json
Emit the versioned deterministic report as JSON. JSON mode never prompts.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Explicitly request non-mutating report behavior.
.TP
.BI "--root " path
Add one bounded worktree pool root. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI "--project-root " path
Add one bounded project root whose repositories may contain
.IR .claude/worktrees .
.TP
.BI "--exclude-root " path
Exclude one root subtree. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI "--only " state
Limit output to one stable sweep state.
.TP
.BI "--sort " attribute
Sort by state, size, updated, repository, or path.
.TP
.B --no-sizes
Skip approximate disk-usage calculation.
.TP
.BI "--color " mode
Use auto, always, or never color behavior. NO_COLOR also disables color.
.TP
.BI "--config " path
Use one explicit versioned YAML config.
.TP
.BI "--jobs " number
Bound concurrent work such as disk-size calculation.
.TP
.BI "--timeout " duration
Bound GitHub evidence collection per repository.
.TP
.B --verbose
Include classification reasons and details in human output.
.TP
.BI "--explain " path-or-id
Explain one matching candidate without applying changes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GIT_WT_ROOT
Override
.IR ~/worktrees ,
primarily for testing.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Controls the optional Kura config root. Sweep reads
.IR kura/git-wt.yaml .
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Controls persisted redacted sweep reports beneath
.IR kura/git-wt/sweeps .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI color in sweep output.
.SH SAFETY
Detached
.B PR-<number>
lanes are inspection-only; use
.B repair
for edits. Writable lanes link the primary checkout's
.B .env
and
.B .envrc
by default when each exists; use
.B --no-link-env
to omit both links for isolation. Existing destination
.B .envrc
files are preserved.
.PP
The
.B remove
command never forces, deletes a branch, or discards dirty or unpushed state.
Sync may discard only an actual ignored root
.B bin/
directory after merged-pull-request and exact-head proof. Other ignored paths,
nested bin directories, symlinks, tracked changes, and ordinary untracked files
remain protected. No command stashes, resets, cleans, or force-removes
worktrees during ordinary remove, sync, or automatic sweep.
.PP
Sweep treats primary, current, default-branch, locked, positively active,
detached, fork-backed, wrong-base, open, closed-unmerged, missing, ambiguous,
and GitHub-unavailable worktrees as non-selectable. Automatic sweep never
forces. A human may explicitly select a GitHub-merged lane containing local
files or commits only after reviewing its exact paths, OIDs, commits, and
recovery loss; sweep revalidates that snapshot before its one confirmed force
operation. Remote branches are never deleted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-worktree (1)
